10:46:00 | INFO | 🤖 Target initial answer: Head lice don’t usually drown in a normal bath because they can close their breathing openings (spiracles) and survive without fresh air for quite a while. Their bodies and claws also help them cling tightly to hair, and water alone doesn’t wash them off easily. They may remain alive underwater for several hours, and lice eggs (nits) are firmly glued to hair shafts and are also not reliably killed by bathing or swimming. Effective treatment usually requires a properly used lice treatment product plus combing with a fine-toothed nit comb, often repeated according to the product instructions.
